WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
Picture a hotel room in Europe
that costs 100 euros a night.

2
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.590
At the average exchange rate for 2021,

3
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.090
that room cost an American
visitor about 118 dollars.

4
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:16.130
At the 2022 average, about 105 dollars.

5
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.480
The hotel did not cut its price.

6
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.000
The dollar simply bought
more euros than before.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.270
Nobody sets the price
of a dollar or a euro.

8
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.330
So what decides it from
one day to the next?

9
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.170
In this mission, you'll
draw the graph that explains

10
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.650
the price of a dollar.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.060
Then you'll move interest rates
and import spending yourself,

12
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.710
and predict where the exchange rate lands.

13
00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: find out what
makes the dollar rise or fall.
